(* newspeak-spec.pdf 3.1.1: a slot of a value may hold only another value,
   and a class object is one exactly when its enclosing object is -- its
   only state (6.1); a metaclass shares its class's enclosing object and so
   its verdict (`interpreter/instantiate.rs`'s `class_object_is_a_value`).
   `Plain` is nested in a `Wrapper`, an ordinary object, so `Wrapper new
   Plain class` -- Plain's metaclass -- is no value either, and `Holder`
   refuses it, naming the metaclass as `Heap::describe`'s `class_display_name`
   does: "the class Plain class", not "the class class side", which every
   metaclass's mixin is literally named (`heap.rs`'s `describe`,
   `ObjectData::Class` arm). A class nested in the value module itself is
   accepted, which the line before the refusal records.

   The module is a value (`Object <: Value`) because §3.1.1 asks a value
   class's enclosing object to be one; the transcript is therefore read
   from `platform` where it is used, never held in a slot. *)
class ValueSlotNamesARefusedMetaclass = Object <: Value () (
    public class Wrapper = Object new () (
        public class Plain = Object new () ()
    )
    public class Accepted = Value new () ()
    public class Holder of: aClass = Value new (
        | public held = aClass. |
    ) ()
    public main: platform args: arguments = (
        platform transcript show: (Holder of: Accepted) held printString; newLine.
        platform transcript show: (Holder of: Wrapper new Plain class) printString; newLine.
    )
) : ()
